/-!
# Maximal ideals of different heights in a Jacobson Noetherian domain

A Noetherian local ring has a well-defined dimension, and in a Jacobson ring every prime is an
intersection of maximal ideals; one might hope that the localizations of a Jacobson Noetherian
domain at its maximal ideals all had the same dimension. They need not: there is a Jacobson,
universally catenary, Noetherian domain with a maximal ideal whose local ring is one-dimensional
and another whose local ring is two-dimensional.

The mechanism is semilocalization. Over a field `K` take `R = K[x][y]` and the primes
`𝔭 = (y)` of height one and `𝔮 = (y - 1, x)` of height two; semilocalizing `R` at the
multiplicative set `𝔭ᶜ ∩ 𝔮ᶜ` makes both of them maximal while preserving their heights, but the
resulting ring is semilocal, hence not Jacobson. To repair that, adjoin one more variable `t`,
semilocalize at the two primes generated by `𝔭` resp. `𝔮` together with `t`, and then invert
`t`: the variable `t` lies in the Jacobson radical before the last step, so Tag 0GED makes the
localization Jacobson, while the primes generated by `𝔭` and `𝔮` become maximal of the same
heights as before. Excellence survives every step and gives universal catenarity.

## Main results

* `IsLocalization.isMaximal_map_of_inf_primeCompl` and
  `IsLocalization.map_mem_jacobson_bot_of_inf_primeCompl`: in a semilocalization at two primes
  the retained primes become maximal, and an element of both of them lands in the Jacobson
  radical.
* `IsLocalization.exists_maximalSpectrum_height_eq_of_away_of_inf_primeCompl`: a prime
  immediately below one of the two retained primes becomes maximal, of unchanged height, after
  semilocalizing and then inverting an element of the retained prime above it.
* `exists_isJacobsonRing_isExcellent_maximalSpectrum_height_eq`: two maximal heights of an
  excellent Noetherian domain are realized by maximal ideals of a *Jacobson* excellent
  Noetherian domain.
* `exists_isJacobsonRing_isUniversallyCatenary_localization_ringKrullDim_one_and_two`:
  **Stacks 0EEI**, the counterexample itself.

## Implementation notes

The ring, together with its commutative-ring, Noetherian and domain structures, is produced as
an existential witness, as are the two maximal ideals; they are elements of `MaximalSpectrum`,
so that maximality is carried with them. The dimensions are the `ringKrullDim` of the
localizations at those maximal ideals, which `IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height`
identifies with the heights of the ideals.

The coefficient field is `ULift ℚ`, so that the witness is produced in any requested universe.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EEI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EEI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GED](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GED), which makes the
  localization Jacobson
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07QU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07QU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07QW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07QW)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

/-- The contraction of an ideal `I` of `A` along evaluation at an element of `A` lies over `I`:
evaluation is a retraction of the structure map `A → A[X]`. -/
theorem Polynomial.liesOver_comap_evalRingHom {A : Type*} [CommRing A] (a : A) (I : Ideal A) :
    (I.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom a)).LiesOver I := by
  refine ⟨?_⟩
  ext x
  simp [Ideal.mem_comap, Polynomial.algebraMap_eq]

namespace Ideal

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (p q : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] [q.IsPrime]

/-- The multiplicative set of elements outside both of two primes is disjoint from the first. -/
theorem disjoint_inf_primeCompl_left :
    Disjoint ((p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl : Submonoid R) : Set R) (p : Set R) :=
  Set.disjoint_left.mpr fun _ hx hp => hx.1 hp

/-- The multiplicative set of elements outside both of two primes is disjoint from the second. -/
theorem disjoint_inf_primeCompl_right :
    Disjoint ((p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl : Submonoid R) : Set R) (q : Set R) :=
  Set.disjoint_left.mpr fun _ hx hq => hx.2 hq

end Ideal

namespace IsLocalization

variable {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]

/-- Every prime of a semilocalization at two primes lies over an ideal contained in one of
them: the two primes are the only obstructions left in the multiplicative set. -/
theorem under_le_or_under_le_of_inf_primeCompl (p q : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] [q.IsPrime]
    [IsLocalization (p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl) S] (J : Ideal S) [J.IsPrime] :
    J.under R ≤ p ∨ J.under R ≤ q := by
  classical
  apply Ideal.subset_union.mp
  intro x hx
  by_contra h
  have hxS : x ∈ p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl := by
    simpa only [Submonoid.mem_inf, Ideal.mem_primeCompl_iff, Set.mem_union,
      SetLike.mem_coe, not_or] using h
  exact Set.disjoint_left.mp
    ((isPrime_iff_isPrime_disjoint
      (p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl) S J).mp inferInstance).2 hxS hx

/-- In a semilocalization at two incomparable primes, each of the two becomes maximal. -/
theorem isMaximal_map_of_inf_primeCompl (p q : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] [q.IsPrime]
    [IsLocalization (p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl) S] (hpq : ¬ p ≤ q) :
    (p.map (algebraMap R S)).IsMaximal := by
  have hdis := Ideal.disjoint_inf_primeCompl_left p q
  have hpS : (p.map (algebraMap R S)).IsPrime :=
    isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint (p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl) S p inferInstance hdis
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hpm⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal _ hpS.ne_top
  have := hm
  have hpunder : p ≤ m.under R := Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp hpm
  have hmunder : m.under R ≤ p :=
    (under_le_or_under_le_of_inf_primeCompl p q m).resolve_right
      fun h => hpq (hpunder.trans h)
  have heq : p.map (algebraMap R S) = m := by
    rw [← map_under (p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl) S m]
    exact congrArg (Ideal.map (algebraMap R S)) (le_antisymm hpunder hmunder)
  exact heq.symm ▸ hm

/-- An element of both of two primes becomes a member of the Jacobson radical of a
semilocalization at them: by `IsLocalization.under_le_or_under_le_of_inf_primeCompl` every
maximal ideal of the semilocalization lies over one of the two primes. -/
theorem map_mem_jacobson_bot_of_inf_primeCompl (p q : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] [q.IsPrime]
    [IsLocalization (p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl) S] {f : R}
    (hfp : f ∈ p) (hfq : f ∈ q) : algebraMap R S f ∈ (⊥ : Ideal S).jacobson := by
  apply Ideal.mem_sInf.mpr
  rintro m ⟨_, hm⟩
  have := hm
  have hmem (r : Ideal R) [r.IsPrime]
      (hrdis : Disjoint ((p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl : Submonoid R) : Set R) (r : Set R))
      (hr : m.under R ≤ r) (hfr : f ∈ r) : algebraMap R S f ∈ m := by
    have hprime := isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint
      (p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl) S r inferInstance hrdis
    have heq := hm.eq_of_le hprime.ne_top (by
      rw [← map_under (p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl) S m]
      exact Ideal.map_mono hr)
    rw [heq]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hfr
  rcases under_le_or_under_le_of_inf_primeCompl p q m with h | h
  · exact hmem p (Ideal.disjoint_inf_primeCompl_left p q) h hfp
  · exact hmem q (Ideal.disjoint_inf_primeCompl_right p q) h hfq

/-- A prime `r` immediately below one of two retained primes `p` becomes maximal, with its
height unchanged, after semilocalizing at `p` and `q` and then inverting an element `f` of `p`
which does not lie in `r` — provided `r` is not contained in `q`. -/
theorem exists_maximalSpectrum_height_eq_of_away_of_inf_primeCompl
    {A B : Type*} [IsNoetherianRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] (p q r : Ideal R)
    [p.IsPrime] [q.IsPrime] [r.IsPrime] [IsLocalization (p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl) A]
    (f : R) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [IsLocalization.Away (algebraMap R A f) B]
    (hrp : r ≤ p) (hrq : ¬ r ≤ q) (hfp : f ∈ p) (hfr : f ∉ r)
    (hheight : p.height = r.height + 1) :
    ∃ m : MaximalSpectrum B, m.asIdeal.height = r.height := by
  let M := p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl
  let rA := r.map (algebraMap R A)
  have hrdis : Disjoint (M : Set R) (r : Set R) :=
    Set.disjoint_left.mpr fun _ hx hr => hx.1 (hrp hr)
  have : rA.IsPrime := isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint M A r inferInstance hrdis
  have hrunder : rA.under R = r :=
    under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint M A inferInstance hrdis
  have hfA : algebraMap R A f ∉ rA := by
    change f ∉ rA.under R
    rwa [hrunder]
  have hrAdis : Disjoint (Submonoid.powers (algebraMap R A f) : Set A) (rA : Set A) := by
    apply Set.disjoint_left.mpr
    rintro _ ⟨n, rfl⟩ hn
    exact hfA ((inferInstance : rA.IsPrime).mem_of_pow_mem n hn)
  let rB := rA.map (algebraMap A B)
  have : rB.IsPrime :=
    isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint (.powers (algebraMap R A f)) B rA inferInstance hrAdis
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hrm⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal rB (Ideal.IsPrime.ne_top inferInstance)
  have := hm
  let J := (m.under A).under R
  have : (m.under A).IsPrime := inferInstance
  have : J.IsPrime := inferInstance
  have hrJ : r ≤ J := Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp hrm)
  have hJp : J ≤ p := (under_le_or_under_le_of_inf_primeCompl p q (m.under A)).resolve_right
    fun h => hrq (hrJ.trans h)
  have hfJ : f ∉ J := fun h => Set.disjoint_left.mp
    ((isPrime_iff_isPrime_disjoint (.powers (algebraMap R A f)) B m).mp inferInstance).2
    (Submonoid.mem_powers (algebraMap R A f)) h
  have hJlt : J < p := hJp.lt_of_ne fun h => hfJ (h ▸ hfp)
  have hrJeq : r = J := by
    apply le_antisymm hrJ
    by_contra h
    have h₁ := Ideal.height_add_one_le_of_lt_of_isPrime (hrJ.lt_of_not_ge h)
    have h₂ := Ideal.height_strict_mono_of_isPrime hJlt
    rw [hheight] at h₂
    exact (not_lt_of_ge h₁) h₂
  have hrAm : rA = m.under A := by
    rw [← map_under M A (m.under A)]
    change r.map (algebraMap R A) = J.map (algebraMap R A)
    rw [hrJeq]
  have hrBm : rB = m := by
    change rA.map (algebraMap A B) = m
    rw [hrAm, map_under (.powers (algebraMap R A f)) B]
  refine ⟨⟨m, hm⟩, ?_⟩
  change m.height = r.height
  rw [← hrBm, height_map_of_disjoint (.powers (algebraMap R A f)) rA hrAdis,
    height_map_of_disjoint M r hrdis]

end IsLocalization

/-- The kernel of evaluation at `0` on `A[X]` is the principal ideal `(X)`, of height one. -/
private theorem height_ker_evalRingHom_zero {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] :
    (RingHom.ker (Polynomial.evalRingHom (0 : A))).height = 1 := by
  rw [Polynomial.ker_evalRingHom]
  simpa using Ideal.height_span_singleton_eq_one_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors
    (mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_ne_zero.mpr Polynomial.X_ne_zero) Polynomial.not_isUnit_X

/-- Two maximal heights of an excellent Noetherian domain are realized by maximal ideals of a
Jacobson excellent Noetherian domain: adjoin a variable `t`, semilocalize at the two primes
generated by the given maximal ideals together with `t`, and invert `t`. -/
theorem exists_isJacobsonRing_isExcellent_maximalSpectrum_height_eq
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsDomain R]
    (hR : IsExcellent R) (p q : Ideal R) [p.IsMaximal] [q.IsMaximal] (hpq : p ≠ q) :
    ∃ (B : Type u) (_ : CommRing B) (_ : IsNoetherianRing B) (_ : IsDomain B),
      IsJacobsonRing B ∧ IsExcellent B ∧
        ∃ m₁ m₂ : MaximalSpectrum B,
          m₁.asIdeal.height = p.height ∧ m₂.asIdeal.height = q.height := by
  classical
  let P := p.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)
  let Q := q.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)
  have heval : Function.Surjective (Polynomial.evalRingHom (0 : R)) :=
    fun x => ⟨Polynomial.C x, by simp⟩
  let M := P.primeCompl ⊓ Q.primeCompl
  let A := Localization M
  have hM : M ≤ nonZeroDivisors (Polynomial R) :=
    inf_le_left.trans P.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
  have : IsDomain A := IsLocalization.isDomain_localization hM
  let f : A := algebraMap (Polynomial R) A Polynomial.X
  let B := Localization.Away f
  have hf : f ≠ 0 := by
    intro h
    apply Polynomial.X_ne_zero (R := R)
    apply IsLocalization.injective A hM
    simpa only [map_zero] using h
  have : IsDomain B := IsLocalization.isDomain_localization
    (Submonoid.powers_le.mpr (mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_ne_zero.mpr hf))
  have hA : IsExcellent A :=
    (isQuasiExcellent_and_isExcellent_of_essFiniteType (R := Polynomial R) (S := A)).2
      ((isExcellent_of_standard_classes_and_finiteType.2.2.2.2 R (Polynomial R)) hR)
  have hB : IsExcellent B :=
    (isQuasiExcellent_and_isExcellent_of_essFiniteType (R := A) (S := B)).2 hA
  have hfj : f ∈ (⊥ : Ideal A).jacobson :=
    IsLocalization.map_mem_jacobson_bot_of_inf_primeCompl P Q
      (by simp [P, Ideal.mem_comap]) (by simp [Q, Ideal.mem_comap])
  have hJB : IsJacobsonRing B :=
    isJacobsonRing_of_isContainedInJacobson_of_isLocalization_away
      ((⊥ : Ideal A).jacobson) le_rfl f hfj B
  have key (I J : Ideal R) [I.IsMaximal] [J.IsMaximal] (hIJ : ¬ I ≤ J)
      [IsLocalization ((I.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)).primeCompl ⊓
        (J.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)).primeCompl) A] :
      ∃ m : MaximalSpectrum B, m.asIdeal.height = I.height := by
    have := Polynomial.liesOver_comap_evalRingHom (0 : R) I
    have : (I.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)).IsMaximal :=
      Ideal.comap_isMaximal_of_surjective _ heval
    have : (J.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)).IsMaximal :=
      Ideal.comap_isMaximal_of_surjective _ heval
    have hX : (Polynomial.X : Polynomial R) ∉ I.map Polynomial.C := by
      intro h
      have h1 : (1 : R) ∈ I := by simpa using (Ideal.mem_map_C_iff.mp h) 1
      exact Ideal.IsPrime.ne_top inferInstance ((Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).mpr h1)
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ :=
      IsLocalization.exists_maximalSpectrum_height_eq_of_away_of_inf_primeCompl
        (A := A) (B := B) (I.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)) (J.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0))
        (I.map Polynomial.C) Polynomial.X
        (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun _ hx => by simpa [Ideal.mem_comap] using hx)
        (fun h => hIJ fun _ hx => by
          simpa [Ideal.mem_comap] using h (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem Polynomial.C hx))
        (by simp [Ideal.mem_comap]) hX (by
          rw [Polynomial.height_eq_height_add_one I (I.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)),
            Polynomial.height_map_C])
    exact ⟨m, by simpa only [Polynomial.height_map_C] using hm⟩
  have : IsLocalization (Q.primeCompl ⊓ P.primeCompl) A := by
    rw [inf_comm]
    infer_instance
  obtain ⟨m₁, hm₁⟩ := key p q fun h => hpq (Ideal.IsMaximal.eq_of_le inferInstance
    (Ideal.IsMaximal.ne_top inferInstance) h)
  obtain ⟨m₂, hm₂⟩ := key q p fun h => hpq (Ideal.IsMaximal.eq_of_le inferInstance
    (Ideal.IsMaximal.ne_top inferInstance) h).symm
  exact ⟨B, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, hJB, hB, m₁, m₂, hm₁, hm₂⟩

/-- **Stacks 0EEI.** There is a Jacobson, universally catenary, Noetherian domain `B` with
maximal ideals `𝔪₁` and `𝔪₂` such that `dim B_{𝔪₁} = 1` and `dim B_{𝔪₂} = 2`. -/
@[stacks 0EEI, ega "IV 10.7.3" "n = 2 case"]
theorem exists_isJacobsonRing_isUniversallyCatenary_localization_ringKrullDim_one_and_two :
    ∃ (B : Type u) (_ : CommRing B) (_ : IsNoetherianRing B) (_ : IsDomain B),
      IsJacobsonRing B ∧ Ring.IsUniversallyCatenary B ∧
        ∃ m₁ m₂ : MaximalSpectrum B,
          ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime m₁.asIdeal) = 1 ∧
          ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime m₂.asIdeal) = 2 := by
  classical
  let K := ULift.{u} ℚ
  let R := Polynomial (Polynomial K)
  let _ : CommRing R := inferInstance
  let n : Ideal (Polynomial K) := RingHom.ker (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)
  have : n.IsMaximal := RingHom.ker_isMaximal_of_surjective
    (Polynomial.evalRingHom (0 : K)) fun x => ⟨Polynomial.C x, by simp⟩
  have hnht : n.height = 1 := height_ker_evalRingHom_zero
  let p : Ideal R := RingHom.ker (Polynomial.evalRingHom 0)
  let q : Ideal R := n.comap (Polynomial.evalRingHom 1)
  have : p.IsPrime := RingHom.ker_isPrime (Polynomial.evalRingHom (0 : Polynomial K))
  have : q.IsMaximal := Ideal.comap_isMaximal_of_surjective
    (Polynomial.evalRingHom (1 : Polynomial K)) fun x => ⟨Polynomial.C x, by simp⟩
  have := Polynomial.liesOver_comap_evalRingHom (1 : Polynomial K) n
  have hpht : Ideal.height (R := R) p = 1 := height_ker_evalRingHom_zero
  have hqht : Ideal.height (R := R) q = 2 := by
    rw [Polynomial.height_eq_height_add_one n q, hnht]
    norm_num
  have hpq : ¬ p ≤ q := by
    intro h
    have hX : (Polynomial.X : R) ∈ p := by simp [p, RingHom.mem_ker]
    have h1 : (1 : Polynomial K) ∈ n := by simpa [q, R, Ideal.mem_comap] using h hX
    exact Ideal.IsMaximal.ne_top inferInstance ((Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).mpr h1)
  let M := p.primeCompl ⊓ q.primeCompl
  let A := Localization M
  have : IsDomain A := IsLocalization.isDomain_localization
    (show M ≤ nonZeroDivisors R from inf_le_left.trans p.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors)
  have : (p.map (algebraMap R A)).IsMaximal :=
    IsLocalization.isMaximal_map_of_inf_primeCompl p q hpq
  have : (q.map (algebraMap R A)).IsMaximal :=
    IsLocalization.isMaximal_of_isMaximal_disjoint M A q
      (Ideal.disjoint_inf_primeCompl_right p q)
  have hR : IsExcellent R :=
    (isExcellent_of_standard_classes_and_finiteType.2.2.2.2 K R)
      (isExcellent_of_standard_classes_and_finiteType.{u, u}.1 K)
  have hA : IsExcellent A :=
    (isQuasiExcellent_and_isExcellent_of_essFiniteType (R := R) (S := A)).2 hR
  have hpA : (p.map (algebraMap R A)).height = 1 := by
    rw [IsLocalization.height_map_of_disjoint M p
      (Ideal.disjoint_inf_primeCompl_left p q), hpht]
  have hqA : (q.map (algebraMap R A)).height = 2 := by
    rw [IsLocalization.height_map_of_disjoint M q
      (Ideal.disjoint_inf_primeCompl_right p q), hqht]
  obtain ⟨B, iB, nB, dB, hJB, hEB, m₁, m₂, hm₁, hm₂⟩ :=
    exists_isJacobsonRing_isExcellent_maximalSpectrum_height_eq A hA
      (p.map (algebraMap R A)) (q.map (algebraMap R A))
      (fun h => by
        rw [h, hqA] at hpA
        norm_num at hpA)
  exact ⟨B, iB, nB, dB, hJB, hEB.2, m₁, m₂,
    by rw [IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height m₁.asIdeal, hm₁, hpA]; rfl,
    by rw [IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height m₂.asIdeal, hm₂, hqA]; rfl⟩

end
